I installed Python3.14 on the PI.

I use Filezilla to transfer the project's files to the PI, using the credentials listed above.

In the final configuration of the project, the PI is set up with a user service named "ginger."  The configuration file lives in ~/.config/systemd/user/rope_test.service.  The file sets the PYTHONPATH directory to /home/fol/pyroot, and all of the project-specific files live in its subdirectories.  The main program is main.py in "/home/fol/pyroot/ginger".  The PI is configured to start this script automatically after initialization - "autostart".

Some useful commands for initializing autostart, cancelling it, inspecting it, and starting/stopping the "ginger" service:

To make it start on boot requires sending the following commands:
systemctl --user enable ginger
sudo loginctl enable-linger $USER
(The second command only needs to be sent once)

To disable autostart:
systemctl --user disable ginger

Other useful commands, to stop and start the service and check its status:
systemctl --user start ginger
systemctl --user stop ginger
systemctl --user status ginger

To force a reload of the service's config file, after it has changed:
systemctl --user daemon-reload

To check the status of autostart:
systemctl --user list-unit-files | grep ginger

The PixelControllers are at 192.168.1.20 and 192.168.1.21.
20 controls the river lights on ports 9-14, which map to universes 9-21.
20 controls the candy canes on the front of the float, ports 1-8.
21 controls the candy canes on the back of the float, ports 9-12.
21 controls the lights on the eves of the house, ports 15-16.

    
